WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.440
Dependency risks begin with visibility.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.740
Teams need to know what components are used, where they run, who owns them,

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.520
and whether they affect systems that process, store, or transmit CUI.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.940
Unsupported software becomes difficult to defend because security fixes may no longer be

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.080
available. End-of-life frameworks, plugins, runtimes,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.300
and operating systems should be replaced or isolated according to risk.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.840
Third-party components and supply chain dependencies can introduce vulnerabilities or

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.940
malicious behavior. Package sources, build tools, container images,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.520
and vendor software should be governed as part of the application boundary.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.940
Vulnerability response requires prioritization, testing, and timely remediation.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.640
Teams should evaluate exploitability, exposure, compensating controls,

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.340
and business impact while avoiding indefinite patch delays.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.440
Maintain software inventory and ownership.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.620
Use dependency scanning and vulnerability monitoring.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.840
Patch, upgrade, replace, or isolate vulnerable components.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:14.300
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include SI.L2-3.14.1 - Flaw remediation;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.160
CM.L2-3.4.1 - Inventory awareness.
